    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 15th with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns today\u2019s highest efficiency score of 80.98. His matchup against McGreevy is primed for success, bolstered by a 13% SP skill advantage and a 14% boost from a favorable platoon split; as our primary target for stolen bases, his spot atop the lineup provides the necessary volume to capitalize on this matchup. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (66.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.79) remain locked in as elite anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** continues to provide high-floor production despite a neutral park factor, while **Kyle Schwarber**\u2019s 10% order bonus out of the leadoff spot against Prielipp makes him a strong start in a game where his 0.373 xwOBA suggests potential for a multi-hit performance.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card centered on our utility spot, where **Christian Yelich** (52.29) narrowly edged out **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (42.91). While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** offers a strong 0.385 xwOBA, he is currently stifled by a difficult matchup against Seymour and a -16% penalty regarding opposing SP skill. **Christian Yelich** was granted the nod due to the added utility of his stolen base potential\u2014which our model weights heavily\u2014despite his dynamic platoon disadvantage against Wrobleski. We are keeping a close watch on **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.19); while his power profile is significant, he faces a stern test against Schlittler, whose 2.81 xERA creates a substantial -19% SP skill drag that places **Kazuma Okamoto** on the low end of our recommended starters today.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the SP profile of our opponents. **Trea Turner** (63.78) faces Prielipp, but we have tempered his score slightly due to an \"Elite Hold\" warning; Prielipp\u2019s ability to neutralize base runners suggests that while **Trea Turner** remains a must-start, we should adjust expectations for his stolen base output despite his favorable batting order position. Meanwhile, we continue to keep **Colt Keith**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable offensive environments later in the week.",
